Z||000002||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||11:46 AM||||Put the last part you took out in first and the first part you took out in last.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Just kidding ,the chilton manual has some exploded views in it,s body section.<P>What,s the deal with the panel cover laying on the windshield? What is the plan?<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000003||Tina||04-07-2001||11:57 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>What,s the deal with the panel cover laying on the windshield? What is the plan?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Should of seen that coming. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>One of the preliminary templates of my new gauge cluster.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rprevo||04-07-2001||03:43 PM|||| I don't have any pictures but I just did<BR>a Fiero interior swap Brown to grey,<BR>Here is the order that I put mine back together in.<BR>Carpet, Plastic center frame for council,<BR>dash board, seat belts, headliner, The panel<BR>behind the seats then I did the trim that <BR>that runs along the front windshield, rear<BR>trim that covers the seat belts then the<BR>bottom trim at the base of the floorboards.<BR>from there I put the cluster in and the<BR>council. The only plastic clips I had problems finding were the ones along the<BR>trim that connect near the windshield.<BR>I went to a local shop that does interiors<BR>and the guy gave me a couple.<BR> To put the dash in you have   <BR>2 screws under the speaker grill and<BR>2 screws under the dash, One by the fuse box<BR>the other in the same place on the passenger<BR>side. The cluster screws are pretty much<BR>the same size as the screws under the<BR>ashtray that holds the assembly that surrounds the shifter. I hope this helps<BR>I had a hard time at first because I'm not<BR>that good at puzzles.<P>     Ray<BR>||||reg||6
